+# Four-function IPv4 listener advertisement
+
+Status: implemented locally; build and runtime qualification pending.
+
+The patch applies to NCCL73cf112295c33aee2b895f329f592f2a9b4b0f97 with the declared SparkRing switchless-cycle patch. It retains legacy listener-field offsets and uses a112-byte handle. Production compilation checks actual socket/verbs/stage sizes and offsets.
+
+Set `NCCL_IB_EXTENDED_IPV4_GIDS=1` on listeners to advertise up to four strictly IPv4-mapped GIDs. Default0 preserves two-GID publication. Recognized extended handles are decoded regardless of the publication flag, while a zero format retains the original two-GID path without inspecting uninitialized legacy tail bytes. Unknown/nonzero format metadata is rejected before payload reads. Generic IB and IPv6 use legacy publication; overflow beyond four candidates falls back to legacy rather than truncating a versioned list. Existing subnet matching and device-selection policy are unchanged.
+
+Set `NCCL_IB_ROUTE_DIAGNOSTICS=1` with INFO/NET logging for one record per final QP at completed connection setup. Each record names send/receive side, communicator pointer, effective merged device, QP index/number, actual IB device/HCA/port, local/remote GIDs and remote QP number. No records are emitted per connection-progress poll or timed collective. This is connection identity, not a measurement of byte distribution.
+
+CPU-only codec/compatibility check on Linux:
+
+```sh
+c++ -std=c++11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror tests/routing_handle/compat.cc -o /tmp/nccl-routing-handle-test
+/tmp/nccl-routing-handle-test
+```
+
+The test exercises1–4 address round trips, byte order, duplicate addresses, zero-format legacy behavior with poisoned trailing bytes, invalid versions/families/counts before payload access, mixed IPv6 fallback and unchanged legacy prefix fields. The full NCCL translation unit must also compile with the actual AArch64 headers; the lightweight test's layout replica does not replace production static assertions.
+
+Before timing, qualify primary-only, secondary-only and both-domain communicators with changing payload correctness and final route records on all four hosts. Compare extension-disabled/enabled using the same candidate binary. Require secondary-domain QP selection and per-HCA traffic deltas before claiming both domains carried useful bytes. Preserve the existing known-good binary and reject failed connection/correctness gates.
+
+## PCI-root-preserving subnet fallback
+
+`NCCL_IB_PRESERVE_PCI_DOMAIN=1` adds a separate default-off selection preference. An already reachable topology default is unchanged. Otherwise, a fully reachable merged device on the same canonical `pciDDDD:BB` root is preferred before the original global first-match fallback. Every PF in both merged devices must have a known identical root and be RoCE; mixed-root, unknown-path and non-RoCE groups retain the existing global fallback. A failed GID query or any unreachable member disqualifies a preferred candidate. This does not alter advertisement, protocols, channel counts or per-collective submission.
+
+The CPU test verifies canonical root parsing, distinct primary/secondary roots, merged-member agreement, malformed/unknown paths and null handling. Full connection correctness and final-QP distribution require the isolated four-rank runtime test. A root key is a PCI root complex, not a promise of measured bandwidth.
diff --git a/tests/routing_handle/compat.cc b/tests/routing_handle/compat.cc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2cb2f00
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/routing_handle/compat.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+// CPU-only codec and legacy-prefix compatibility test. No CUDA or NIC required.
+#include "../../src/transport/net_ib/routing_handle.h"
+#include "../../src/transport/net_ib/routing_pci_root.h"
+#include <assert.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <netinet/in.h>
+
+union Address { sockaddr sa; sockaddr_in sin; sockaddr_in6 sin6; };
+union Gid { uint8_t raw[16]; uint64_t alignment[2]; };
+struct Stage { int state; int offset; void* buffer; void* comm; };
+struct Legacy { Address address; uint64_t magic; Stage stage; Gid gids[2]; };
+struct Extended { Address address; uint8_t format[4]; uint64_t magic; Stage stage;
+                  Gid gids[2]; uint8_t ips[4][4]; };
+static_assert(sizeof(Legacy) == 96 && sizeof(Extended) == 112, "LP64 layout required");
+static_assert(offsetof(Extended, format) == 28 && offsetof(Extended, magic) == 32 &&
+              offsetof(Extended, stage) == 40 && offsetof(Extended, gids) == 64 &&
+              offsetof(Extended, ips) == 96, "Legacy offsets changed");
+
+int main() {
+  uint8_t gids[4][16] = {};
+  for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+    gids[i][10] = gids[i][11] = 0xff;
+    gids[i][12] = 192; gids[i][13] = 168; gids[i][14] = (uint8_t)(101+i); gids[i][15] = 10;
+  }
+  for (int count = 1; count <= 4; count++) {
+    Extended handle = {};
+    memcpy(handle.gids, gids, 32);
+    Legacy prefix; memcpy(&prefix, &handle, sizeof(prefix));
+    assert(ncclIbRoutingEncodeIpv4(handle.format, handle.ips, gids, count) == count);
+    uint8_t decoded[4][16]; memset(decoded, 0xa5, sizeof(decoded));
+    assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(handle.format, handle.ips, decoded) == count);
+    assert(memcmp(decoded, gids, count*16) == 0);
+    assert(memcmp(prefix.gids, handle.gids, 32) == 0);
+    assert(handle.magic == prefix.magic && handle.stage.state == prefix.stage.state);
+    // An old consumer retains identical socket/magic/stage/two-GID fields.
+    Legacy old; memcpy(&old, &handle, sizeof(old));
+    assert(memcmp(old.gids, gids, 32) == 0);
+    // The opaque exchange remains bounded by 128 bytes with untouched guards.
+    alignas(8) uint8_t exchange[144]; memset(exchange, 0xa7, sizeof(exchange));
+    memcpy(exchange+8, &handle, sizeof(handle));
+    for (int b = 0; b < 8; b++) assert(exchange[b] == 0xa7);
+    for (int b = 136; b < 144; b++) assert(exchange[b] == 0xa7);
+    Extended received; memcpy(&received, exchange+8, sizeof(received));
+    assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(received.format, received.ips, decoded) == count);
+  }
+  for (int poison = 1; poison < 256; poison++) {
+    alignas(8) uint8_t opaque[128]; memset(opaque, poison, sizeof(opaque));
+    memset(opaque, 0, sizeof(Legacy)); // Exact old producer, unknown trailing bytes.
+    assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(opaque + 28, nullptr, nullptr) == 0);
+  }
+  uint8_t format[4], ips[4][4], decoded[4][16];
+  const int badCounts[] = {-1, 0, 5, 255};
+  for (int badCount : badCounts) {
+    assert(ncclIbRoutingEncodeIpv4(format, ips, nullptr, badCount) == 0);
+    assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(format, nullptr, nullptr) == 0);
+  }
+  for (int field = 0; field < 4; field++) {
+    assert(ncclIbRoutingEncodeIpv4(format, ips, gids, 4) == 4);
+    format[field] = 255;
+    assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(format, nullptr, nullptr) == -1);
+  }
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingEncodeIpv4(format, ips, gids, 4) == 4);
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(format, nullptr, decoded) == -1);
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(format, ips, nullptr) == -1);
+  format[3] = 0;
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(format, nullptr, nullptr) == -1);
+  uint8_t ipv6[4][16]; memcpy(ipv6, gids, sizeof(ipv6)); ipv6[2][0] = 0x20;
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingEncodeIpv4(format, ips, ipv6, 4) == 0);
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(format, nullptr, nullptr) == 0);
+  memcpy(gids[3], gids[0], 16); // Duplicate reachable addresses round-trip unchanged.
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingEncodeIpv4(format, ips, gids, 4) == 4);
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingDecodeIpv4(format, ips, decoded) == 4);
+  assert(memcmp(decoded, gids, 64) == 0);
+  const char* primary[] = {"/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:00.0/0000:01:00.0",
+                           "/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:00.0/0000:01:00.1"};
+  const char* secondary[] = {"/sys/devices/pci0002:00/0002:00:00.0/0002:01:00.0",
+                             "/sys/devices/pci0002:00/0002:00:00.0/0002:01:00.1"};
+  char pRoot[11], sRoot[11];
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingCommonPciRoot(primary, 2, pRoot));
+  assert(ncclIbRoutingCommonPciRoot(secondary, 2, sRoot));
+  assert(strcmp(pRoot, "pci0000:00") == 0 && strcmp(sRoot, "pci0002:00") == 0);
+  assert(strcmp(pRoot, sRoot) != 0);
+  const char* mixed[] = {primary[0], secondary[0]};
+  assert(!ncclIbRoutingCommonPciRoot(mixed, 2, pRoot));
+  const char* missing[] = {primary[0], nullptr};
+  assert(!ncclIbRoutingCommonPciRoot(missing, 2, pRoot));
+  assert(!ncclIbRoutingCommonPciRoot(primary, 0, pRoot));
+  assert(!ncclIbRoutingCommonPciRoot(nullptr, 2, pRoot));
+  const char* invalidPaths[] = {"", "pci0000:00/0000:01:00.0", "/pci0000:00",
+                               "/sys/devices/pci00000:00/x", "/sys/devices/pci0000:0g/x",
+                               "/sys/devices/platform/roce0", "/pci/x"};
+  for (const char* path : invalidPaths) assert(!ncclIbRoutingPciRoot(path, pRoot));
+  assert(!ncclIbRoutingPciRoot(nullptr, pRoot));
+  assert(!ncclIbRoutingPciRoot(primary[0], nullptr));
+  puts("routing handle codec, PCI root, and legacy compatibility: passed");
+}
